Hi Norm and Claudia,

If Shawn and Charles (and other HP folks) do not travel, due to HP
policy (which Bob Taylor advised us at PWG SM telecon might get bent
on a case-by-case basis), we have a severe shortage of discussion
leaders for the various FSG OP sessions.

While plane tickets are generally non-refundable, it's unlikely
that waiting to the last moment will make the cancellation charges
for the meeting rooms and other facilities cheaper.

FSG OP is morally bound to cover those hotel cancellation charges.

I suggest that a revised agenda of discussion leaders who _think_
they will travel to Washington, DC is necessary for FSG OP to avoid
this cancellation.  And there is also the issue of a "quorum", if
very few FSG OP people will be travelling to Washington, DC.

Cheers,
